course: dictionary
lesson: 5337
title: A word from history: khanate
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words come from history books, and the sentences around them tell you what they mean. Read the clues. «By 1337 the Mongol world had split into separate khanates such as the Yuan, the Golden Horde and the Ilkhanate.» The sentence lists places, so a khanate must be a kind of place, not a person or a thing you can hold.
explain: The clue «the Ilkhanate in Persia was falling apart» tells you more. Khanates were states, so a khanate can break up, just as a country can. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A khanate is a land or state ruled by a khan.
explain: Khan is a title for a ruler. Khanate is the land or state that the khan rules. Khanate can also mean the power or rule of a khan, so in «the Crimean Khanate», it names a whole kingdom, not one person.
fact: A khan is a ruler of Mongol or Turkic peoples.
fact: A khanate is a land or state ruled by a khan.
fact: Khanate can also mean the power or rule of a khan.
fact: Phrases you may see in history are «the Crimean Khanate» and «the Khanate of Kazan».
exercise: «By 1337 the Mongol world had split into separate khanates such as the Yuan, the Golden Horde and the Ilkhanate.» What is a khanate? | A ship that sails the sea | A kind of horse used in battle | *A land or state ruled by a khan | A large feast held in spring
exercise: «The Ilkhanate in Persia was falling apart.» What does falling apart suggest about the Ilkhanate? | *It was breaking into pieces and losing its strength | It was being built from new stone | It had just been painted | It was getting bigger and stronger
exercise: «But at its start in 1337 the Mongol peace that had made the roads safe was already breaking into rival khanates.» Find and copy one word in this sentence that means competitors who are against each other. | *rival | start | safe | roads
test: «The Crimean Khanate» was a place in history. What is a khanate? | A river crossing | *A land or state ruled by a khan | A rule that nobody may vote | A ruler's cloak
test: Khanate can mean two things. Which is the second meaning? | *The power or rule of a khan | A fight between friends | A tent made of felt | A wide sea of grass
exam: Jayden reads «the Ilkhanate in Persia» and asks what kind of place it was. What is the best answer? | A mountain pass used by travellers | A market for spices | *A kingdom ruled by a khan | A kind of Persian rug
